# The Marriage of the Humanities and the Trades.

**Authors:** Koehnline, William A.

## Abstract
Summarizes interviews with philosophy, electronics, data processing, and radiology students about the humanities. Decries the false dichotomy established in the literature between humanities and vocational education. Illustrates three methods of "marrying" humanities and occupational education: free-standing humanities electives; humanities modules within occupational programs; and inservice, mid-career, or preretirement courses. (DD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ244435

